<title>GREECE: U.S. EMBASSY CLOSED ON MONDAY, FEB 17 FOR PRESIDENT'S DAY.</title>
<headline>U.S. EMBASSY CLOSED ON MONDAY, FEB 17 FOR PRESIDENT'S DAY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. embassy in Athens, the U.S. consulates in Athens and Thessaloniki and all U.S. government offices will be closed on Monday February 17 in observance of the President's Day, the embassy said.</p>
<p>Monday marks the birthdays of Presidents' George Washington and Abraham Lincoln. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
